### Count discovered manifests before applying exclusions (1/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

The zero-manifest guard needs the number of files discovered, not only the files selected for auditing. When a target contains manifests that are intentionally excluded, counting after filtering incorrectly reports that no deps.json files were found. Preserve the discovery count before removing excluded files.

```suggestion
        var files = new List<string>(Directory.EnumerateFiles(root, "*.deps.json", options));
        var scannedFilesCount = files.Count;
        files.RemoveAll(f => IsExcluded(f, Path.GetFileName(f)));
```

### Distinguish absent runtime data from malformed package values (3/4)

**Severity:** `medium`

A package with no `runtime` property is valid and may be skipped, but a non-object package or a present non-object `runtime` value is malformed. The combined condition treats all of these cases as absent data and can hide DLL references; skip only the absent property and reject invalid present values.

```suggestion
                    if (package.Value.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object)
                    {
                        throw new InvalidDataException($"Invalid deps.json structure in {path}: package '{package.Name}' must be an object.");
                    }

                    if (!package.Value.TryGetProperty("runtime", out var runtime))
                    {
                        continue;
                    }

                    if (runtime.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object)
                    {
                        throw new InvalidDataException($"Invalid deps.json structure in {path}: package '{package.Name}' has a non-object runtime value.");
```

### Reject malformed DLL entries and non-string versions (4/4)

**Severity:** `medium`

A DLL runtime entry with a non-object value is skipped, and a present non-string `fileVersion` is converted to an empty string. Either malformed shape can therefore pass when no valid conflict is found; continue only when `fileVersion` is absent and reject invalid entry/value types.

```suggestion
                        if (entry.Value.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object)
                        {
                            throw new InvalidDataException($"Invalid deps.json structure in {path}: DLL runtime entry '{entry.Name}' must be an object.");
                        }

                        if (!entry.Value.TryGetProperty("fileVersion", out var fv))
                        {
                            continue;
                        }

                        if (fv.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.String)
                        {
                            throw new InvalidDataException($"Invalid deps.json structure in {path}: DLL runtime entry '{entry.Name}' has a non-string fileVersion.");
                        }

                        string version = fv.GetString();
```
